ume UBI image with valid EC/VID headers and UBIFS volumes — building a real UBIFS filesystem image synthetically is hard. Better: use ubireader? No, ubireader only extracts. mtd-utils (mkfs.ubifs/ubinize) not available and can't install via package manager...\n\nWait — can I build UBIFS images in pure Python? There might be existing fixtures I can reuse: fruits.ubi (multi-volume: apple + data volumes!) and orange.ubi.truncated.img. If I can fetch those from LFS, I can:\n- Use fruits.ubi as the multi-volume test.\n- Create a bad-block variant by corrupting/erasing a PEB in the middle (simulating a bad block) with a script.\n\nThat covers \"坏块与多卷\" fixtures without needing mkfs.ubifs.\n\nLet me check .gitattributes and try fetching LFS objects via media.githubusercontent.com."]},"started_at_ms":1794659419904,"completed_at_ms":1794659434946}}
