{"timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:39:35.256Z","ordinal":257,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d9fc-8ce9-7420-953c-6c7a3fab8a59","turn_id":"01a1d9fc-8cfb-7500-aadc-dd421289bedc","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_122bcd73ce6b940babe0f6a5","summary_text":[],"raw_content":["fruits.ubi: PEB size = 1024? EC header at 0: vid_hdr_offset=0x40, data_offset=0x80, image_seq=0x465be12b. VID header at 0x40 (\"UBI!\"). Volume table record at 0x128: \"apple\" (name at offset 0x138?), and at 0x1d8: \"data\". VTBL rec size = 128. So PEB0 = layout volume with 2 vtbl records (apple vol_id 0, data vol_id 1). PEB size: let me figure — file is 4096 = 4 PEBs of 1024? EC headers at 0, 1024, 2048, 3072? Let me check: xxd showed only first 0x270. Volume data PEBs contain \"apple1\\n\" etc.\n\nGreat — I can write a generator script mimicking this: PEB size 1024, vid_hdr_offset 0x40, data_offset 0x80. Layout volume PEB (2 copies typically, but fruits has 1?), then data PEBs with VID headers (vol_id, lnum) and data.\n\nStructure of VID header (64 bytes): magic \"UBI!\", version 1, vol_type (1=dynamic? fruits shows 01 01 00 05: version=1, vol_type=1, copy_flag=0, compat=5), vol_id (0x7fffefff = UBI_LAYOUT_VOLUME_ID 0x7fffefff), lnum, ... data_crc, etc., hdr_crc at offset 60.\n\nLet me parse fruits.ubi fully with a Python script to get exact layout, then write the fixture generator. Actually simpler: write the generator using ubireader's own structs? ubireader has headers.ec_hdr/vid_hdr/vtbl_recs packing functions? It has struct formats; I can use struct directly.\n\nPlan of files to write:\n\n1. `python/unblob/handlers/filesystem/ubi.py` — rework:\n   - UBIHandler → StructHandler with EC header C definition, local GCD PEB size guess, bad-block-tolerant walk with EC header CRC validation, updated HandlerDoc (description + limitations).\n   - UBIFSHandler → add superblock field validation, updated HandlerDoc.\n2. `tests/handlers/filesystem/test_ubi.py` — unit tests.\n3. New integration fixture: `tests/integration/filesystem/ubi/ubi/__input__/fruits-badblock.ubi` (multi-volume + bad PEB) + expected `__output__`. Generate with a script; run the integration test to produce output, verify, copy.\n4. Regenerate `docs/handlers.md`.\n5. README already lists UBI/UBIFS — check docs/format list elsewhere? \"格式列表\" = docs/handlers.md table probably. It's generated. Good.\n\nWait — should the new fixture go under `ubi/ubi/__input__`? Yes, tests/integration/filesystem/ubi/ubi/ (module ubi, handler NAME ubi). Adding a new input file there means expected output dir `fruits-badblock.ubi_extract/`.\n\nAlso: CRC32 for UBI headers: crc32(data) with init 0 (UBI_CRC32_INIT = 0)? ubireader: `crc32(buf, 0)`? Let me check ubireader's crc32 usage: UBI_CRC32_INIT = 0. Python zlib.crc32(data, 0) & 0xffffffff. Kernel: crc32(UBI_CRC32_INIT, buf, len) with UBI_CRC32_INIT = ~0? Hmm. Kernel ubi-media.h: `#define UBI_CRC32_INIT 0xFFFFFFFFU`? Let me check ubireader source: UBI_CRC32_INIT value. Let me verify by computing CRC of fruits.ubi EC header: hdr_crc at offset 0x3c = 0x3763f3bc. Compute zlib.crc32 of first 60 bytes with different inits and compare.\n\nLet me now write a scratch script to parse fruits.ubi and verify CRC scheme."]},"started_at_ms":1794659947640,"completed_at_ms":1794659975256}}
