{"timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:42:41.345Z","ordinal":284,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d9fc-8ce9-7420-953c-6c7a3fab8a59","turn_id":"01a1d9fc-8cfb-7500-aadc-dd421289bedc","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_cf2a178f67f0be67b00a778b","summary_text":[],"raw_content":["Hmm wait, the vtbl recs I parsed at offset 128 are wrong — earlier xxd showed \"apple\" at 0x138 (312) and \"data\" at 0x1e2. The vtbl records start at data_off=128, each 172 bytes: rec0 at 128..300, rec1 at 300..472. \"apple\" at 0x138=312... that's inside rec1? 128+172=300; name field offset within rec = 4+4+4+1+1+2=16 → 300+16=316? Hmm xxd showed at 0x130: `0000 0001 0000 0000 0200 0005 6170 706c` at 0x12c-0x13a: reserved_pebs=1? Let me not worry — my parse shows VTBL0 empty, VTBL1 = apple... but there should be a \"data\" record too. Wait xxd at 0x1d0: `b6d2 9067 0000 0001 0000 0001 0000 0000 0100 0004 6461 7461` → at 0x1d4: crc, then 0x1d8: reserved_pebs=1, alignment=1, data_pad=0, vol_type=1, upd=0, name_len=4, \"data\". So rec1 (at 300=0x12c): reserved_pebs=1 (0x12c: 0000 0001), alignment=1, vol_type=2 (static), name \"apple\". rec2 at 472=0x1d8: reserved_pebs=1, vol_type=1 (dynamic), name \"data\". So there are 3 records? rec0 at 128 empty, rec1 apple (vol_id... index 1 → vol_id 1), rec2 data (vol_id 2). And PEB2 has vol_id=1 (apple, static, data \"apple1\\n\"), PEB3 vol_id=2 (data, dynamic, but data_size=0 with \"cherry1\\n\" content?).\n\nHmm interesting — PEB3 vol_type=1 dynamic, data_size=0, but contains \"cherry1\\n\". And expected output `img-1180426539_vol-data.ubifs` — let me check its content. And vol-apple.ubifs content \"apple1\\n\". Wait, image_seq 0x465be12b = 1180426539? 0x465be12b = 1180426539. Yes!\n\nSo ubireader output for dynamic volume with data_size=0... the vol-data.ubifs output file — check content. Whatever — the fixture works today; I'll mimic this structure for my new fixture but I don't need to replicate quirks. Actually simplest robust approach for the new fixture: build a *valid* image with my generator and verify ubireader extracts it.\n\nDesign `multi-volume-badblock.ubi` (name: maybe `fruits-badblock.ubi`? Better descriptive: `multi_volume_bad_blocks.ubi`):\n- PEB size 1024, 10 PEBs.\n- PEB0, PEB1: layout volume copies (vol_id 0x7fffefff, lnum 0 and 1) with vtbl: 2 volumes: \"config\" (vol_id 1, static? dynamic) and \"rootfs\"... let me keep two dynamic volumes \"alpha\" (vol_id 1) and \"beta\" (vol_id 2), each 1-2 LEBs of raw text data.\n- PEB2: alpha LEB0 (vol_id 1, lnum 0, data \"alpha1\\n\")\n- PEB3: BAD BLOCK — garbage (no valid EC header). Simulates bad PEB.\n- PEB4: alpha LEB1 (vol_id 1, lnum 1, data \"alpha2\\n\")\n- PEB5: beta LEB0 (vol_id 2, lnum 0, data \"beta1\\n\")\n- PEB6: BAD BLOCK (0xff-filled)\n- PEB7: beta LEB1 (vol_id 2, lnum 1, data \"beta2\\n\")\n- PEB8,9: maybe trailing bad blocks at end? Also good to test: end with bad blocks → chunk end = last valid PEB end = 8*1024? If PEB8,9 are bad, chunk end = 8192, file size 10240. Then output chunk 0-8192.ubi. Hmm, that leaves 8192-10240 unknown — fine, shows in output as .unknown file. Maybe keep file exactly ending after last valid PEB to keep output clean. Let me make PEB8: alpha LEB2? Not needed. Keep 8 PEBs total (0..7), ending with valid PEB7.\n\nWait, but should the bad PEBs be *unallocated*? In real UBI, bad PEBs are skipped during wear-leveling; LEBs map around them. My layout does exactly that (LEBs on PEBs 2,4,5,7; bad at 3,6). \n\nExpected ubireader behavior: extracts img-<seq>_vol-alpha.ubifs and _vol-beta.ubifs. What will the .ubifs content be? ubireader writes LEB data sequentially per volume: alpha = \"alpha1\\n\" + \"alpha2\\n\" (LEB data concatenated, each LEB padded to leb_size?). leb_size = peb_size - data_offset = 1024-128 = 896. ubireader writes data_size bytes or full LEB? For dynamic volumes, data_size bytes per LEB. Output files will be tiny. Since volumes aren't real UBIFS, no further extraction. Output mirrors fruits.ubi style. \n\nOld handler on this fixture: walk stops at PEB3 (bad) → chunk 0-3072 → ubireader extracts only alpha LEB0... Actually wait, would old `_guess_peb_size` even work? offsets at 0,1024,2048,(3072 bad),4096,5120,(6144 bad),7168 → intervals [1024,1024,2048,1024,2048,1024] → mode 1024 ✓. Walk: PEB0,1,2 valid, PEB3 bad → stop → chunk 0-3072. New handler: skips PEB3, PEB6 → chunk 0-8192. \n\nAlso unit tests will cover: bad block skip, >20 consecutive bad → stop, gcd peb guess with bad blocks, multi-image different PEB sizes, single PEB → InvalidInputFormat, truncated, UBIFS validation gates.\n\nNow, will ubireader_extract_images handle the bad PEBs? It builds `blocks` from EC headers found... let me just test after generating. One concern: ubireader's own peb-size guess — `ubireader_extract_images` without -p: it uses `guess_peb_size`? Let me check ubireader's ubi_file: it searches for UBI_EC_HDR_MAGIC occurrences... `get_peb_size` looks at first two EC hdr offsets? If it uses file offsets of first two magics found → 0 and 1024 → 1024 ✓.\n\nAlso: does ubireader require the *layout volume* (vtbl) to map volumes? Yes — it reads vtbl_recs from the layout volume to get volume names/IDs. My PEB0/PEB1 provide that (2 copies; ubireader handles 1 or 2).\n\nVTBL record for volume: reserved_pebs (number of PEBs reserved = LEB count), alignment=1, data_pad=0, vol_type=1 (dynamic), upd_marker=0, name_len, name, flags=0, padding, crc = ~crc32(first 168 bytes).\n\nLet me now check how ubireader computes which PEBs belong to a volume: via VID headers (vol_id). Good.\n\nData CRC: for dynamic volumes, data_crc = ~crc32(data[:data_size]). ubireader checks? It may log errors only. Set correctly anyway.\n\nEC header: ec (erase count) = 0, vid_hdr_offset=64, data_offset=128, image_seq = some constant, hdr_crc.\n\nAlright. Also need `sqnum` in VID header — increasing sequence numbers; ubireader uses sqnum to pick latest version of a LEB. Set distinct increasing values.\n\nNow, let me also double check `iterate_patterns` signature and `StructParser.parse` API. Let me read relevant parts of models.py and file_utils."]},"started_at_ms":1794660115657,"completed_at_ms":1794660161345}}
