{"timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:49:59.594Z","ordinal":407,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2349000,"cached_input_tokens":2154496,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":41268,"reasoning_output_tokens":29296,"total_tokens":2390268},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":86793,"cached_input_tokens":81920,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":95,"reasoning_output_tokens":0,"total_tokens":86888},"last_usage_includes_reasoning":false,"model_context_window":1000000},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":null,"secondary":null,"credits":null,"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":null,"rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:50:59.186Z","ordinal":408,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d9fc-8ce9-7420-953c-6c7a3fab8a59","turn_id":"01a1d9fc-8cfb-7500-aadc-dd421289bedc","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_b7923f4bda2a7115cb966daa","summary_text":[],"raw_content":["Baseline green again. Now write unit tests. Let me create `tests/handlers/filesystem/test_ubi.py` with a synthetic image builder.\n\nBuilder design (PEB size 1024, vid_hdr_offset 64, data_offset 128):\n\n```python\nimport struct\nimport zlib\n\nPEB_SIZE = 1024\nIMAGE_SEQ = 0xDEADBEEF\n\ndef ec_header(image_seq=IMAGE_SEQ, ec=0, corrupt_crc=False):\n    hdr = struct.pack(\">4sB3sQIII32s\", b\"UBI#\", 1, b\"\\0\"*3, ec, 64, 128, image_seq, b\"\\0\"*32)\n    crc = zlib.crc32(hdr) ^ 0xFFFFFFFF\n    if corrupt_crc: crc ^= 0xFF\n    return hdr + struct.pack(\">I\", crc)\n\ndef peb(image_seq=IMAGE_SEQ, fill=b\"\\xff\", **kwargs):\n    return (ec_header(image_seq, **kwargs) + fill * PEB_SIZE)[:PEB_SIZE]  # hmm, ec_header is 64 bytes; pad to PEB_SIZE\n\ndef bad_peb(): return b\"\\x00\" * PEB_SIZE  # or garbage\n\ndef ubi_image(peb_count, image_seq=IMAGE_SEQ, bad_pebs=()):\n    ...\n```\n\nTests:\n\n1. `test_calculate_chunk` — 4 valid PEBs → (0, 4096). Embedded at offset: prefix + image → (len(prefix), len(prefix)+4096).\n2. `test_calculate_chunk_with_bad_blocks` — valid, valid, bad, valid, valid → chunk covers all 5 PEBs (0, 5120).\n3. `test_calculate_chunk_stops_after_too_many_bad_blocks` — 2 valid + 21 bad + ... → (0, 2048). Use _MAX_CONSECUTIVE_BAD_PEBS+1 bad PEBs.\n4. `test_calculate_chunk_multiple_images` — image A (3 PEBs, seq1, peb 1024) + image B (4 PEBs, seq2, peb 2048): chunk from 0 → (0, 3072); chunk from 3072 → (3072, 3072+8192). This tests image_seq boundary AND different PEB sizes. Wait — _guess_peb_size for B: candidates ≥ 3072 with valid CRC: B's headers at 3072, 5120, 7168, 9216 → intervals 2048 → gcd 2048 ✓. For A: headers at 0,1024,2048 (seq1), B's at 3072+ (seq2, filtered out by seq) → intervals [1024,1024] → 1024 ✓. Walk A: PEB0,1,2 valid; PEB at 3072: valid CRC but seq2 → break → end 3072 ✓.\n5. `test_calculate_chunk_guesses_peb_size_with_bad_blocks` — intervals [1024, 2048, 1024] (bad block between) → gcd 1024. Covered by test 2 implicitly, but explicit unit test on _guess_peb_size is nice. Maybe skip, covered.\n6. `test_calculate_chunk_truncated` — 3 valid PEBs + partial PEB (half) → (0, 3072).\n7. `test_calculate_chunk_single_peb_fails` — 1 PEB → InvalidInputFormat. Use find_chunks? find_chunks asserts no exception reports... InvalidInputFormat is treated as invalid chunk (not an error report) — search_chunks catches InvalidInputFormat. So find_chunks returns []. Good for rejection tests.\n8. First PEB corrupt CRC but rest valid → chunk covers all (first PEB exempt). \n9. UBIFS handler tests: build synthetic superblock (LE 4096-byte node) → chunk (0, leb_size*leb_cnt). Parametrized rejection test: mutate fields (ch.len, key_hash, key_fmt, default_compr, fmt_version, jhead_cnt, min_io_size not pow2, leb_size misaligned, leb_cnt 0, leb_cnt > max_leb_cnt) → each rejected (find_chunks == []).\n10. Big-endian UBIFS superblock → chunk computed.\n\nFor UBIFS synthetic superblock, build with struct.pack little-endian:\n\n```python\ndef ubifs_sb_node(leb_size=0x1F000, leb_cnt=14, ...):\n    ch = struct.pack(\"<IIQIBB2s\", magic=0x06101831, crc=0, sqnum=0, len=4096, node_type=6, group_type=0, pad)\n    ...\n```\n\nThe pattern requires: magic(4) + [16 bytes] + node_type(0x06) + group_type(00|01|02) + 00 00. ch = magic(4) crc(4) sqnum(8) len(4) = 20 bytes, then node_type at offset 20, group_type 21, padding 22-23. Pattern: `31 18 10 06 [16] 06 (00|01|02) 00 00` — 4 + 16 = 20 → node_type at 20 ✓.\n\nThen sb fields after ch (24 bytes): padding[2], key_hash, key_fmt, flags(4), min_io_size(4), leb_size(4), leb_cnt(4), max_leb_cnt(4), max_bud_bytes(8), log_lebs(4), lpt_lebs(4), orph_lebs(4), jhead_cnt(4), fanout(4), lsave_cnt(4), fmt_version(4), default_compr(2), ... rest padding to 4096.\n\nLet me compute offsets per C_DEFINITIONS:\n- ch: 24 bytes (0-23)\n- padding[2]: 24-25\n- key_hash: 26\n- key_fmt: 27\n- flags: 28-31\n- min_io_size: 32-35\n- leb_size: 36-39\n- leb_cnt: 40-43\n- max_leb_cnt: 44-47\n- max_bud_bytes: 48-55\n- log_lebs: 56-59\n- lpt_lebs: 60-63\n- orph_lebs: 64-67\n- jhead_cnt: 68-71\n- fanout: 72-75\n- lsave_cnt: 76-79\n- fmt_version: 80-83\n- default_compr: 84-85 (uint16)\n- padding1[2]: 86-87\n- rp_uid: 88...\n\nI'll build with struct.pack into a bytearray of 4096.\n\nBuilder:\n\n```python\ndef build_sb_node(*, endian=\"<\", node_len=4096, key_hash=0, key_fmt=0, min_io_size=2048,\n                  leb_size=0x1F000, leb_cnt=14, max_leb_cnt=64, jhead_cnt=1,\n                  fmt_version=4, default_compr=2, group_type=0):\n    magic = 0x06101831\n    node = bytearray(4096)\n    struct.pack_into(f\"{endian}IIQIBB2s\", node, 0, magic, 0, 0, node_len, 6, group_type, b\"\\0\\0\")\n    struct.pack_into(f\"{endian}BB\", node, 26, key_hash, key_fmt)\n    struct.pack_into(f\"{endian}IIII\", node, 32, min_io_size, leb_size, leb_cnt, max_leb_cnt)\n    struct.pack_into(f\"{endian}I\", node, 68, jhead_cnt)\n    struct.pack_into(f\"{endian}I\", node, 80, fmt_version)\n    struct.pack_into(f\"{endian}H\", node, 84, default_compr)\n    return bytes(node)\n```\n\nWait — big-endian magic: pattern BE is `06 10 18 31` — pack_into(\">I\", 0x06101831) gives bytes 06 10 18 31 ✓. LE gives 31 18 10 06 ✓.\n\nFor a valid chunk test: content = sb_node + padding to leb_size*leb_cnt? The chunk is (0, leb_size*leb_cnt) regardless of actual content length — but find_chunks/search_chunks: does unblob drop chunks past EOF in find_chunks? Yes — search_chunks drops chunks that run past the file end. So content must be at least leb_size*leb_cnt bytes. Use small leb_size: min_io_size=8, leb_size=64, leb_cnt=4 → 256 bytes total. leb_size % min_io = 0 ✓. max_leb_cnt=8.\n\nWait leb_size=64 with min_io_size=8: fine for gates.\n\nEmbedded test: prefix + sb + padding → chunk at (len(prefix), len(prefix)+256).\n\nTruncated test: content shorter than leb_size*leb_cnt → find_chunks == [] (chunk dropped as it runs past EOF).\n\nRejection parametrized: mutate kwargs → find_chunks(handler, valid_content_with_mutation) == [].\n\nFor UBI rejection: single PEB → []. Also all-bad image → []? First PEB matched by pattern... an image of 1 valid PEB + 21 bad: _guess_peb_size: valid headers = [PEB0] → no intervals → InvalidInputFormat → []. \n\nAlso test that garbage \"UBI#\" with bad CRC doesn't extend: covered by bad-block tests (bad PEBs are zeros — no magic). Maybe make bad PEBs contain \"UBI#\" + version but wrong CRC to prove CRC gating: `bad_peb = ec_header(corrupt_crc=True) + garbage`. Good idea — proves CRC check works.\n\nAlso a false-positive \"UBI#\" in data region affecting old mode-guess: covered implicitly.\n\nNow, one important check on `find_chunks` for UBI: search_chunks with UBIHandler — patterns match \"UBI#\" + version byte at every PEB → calculate_chunk called at each PEB offset → multiple chunks (each PEB start begins its own \"image\" walk!). E.g. 4-PEB image → chunks at 0..4096, 1024..4096, 2048..4096, 3072..4096? calculate_chunk at offset 1024: _guess_peb_size with start=1024: headers ≥1024: 1024,2048,3072 → gcd 1024 → walk from 1024 → end 4096 → chunk (1024, 4096). So find_chunks returns 4 chunks. In real unblob, the outer chunk (0,4096) wins and inner matches are skipped. For tests, I should assert the first chunk or use calculate_chunk directly. testing.calculate_chunk(handler, content, start_offset) runs calculate_chunk directly — cleaner for these tests. Use `calculate_chunk` helper for most, `find_chunks` for rejection tests.\n\nHmm wait, for rejection tests with find_chunks: content with single PEB (invalid) → pattern matches at 0 → calculate_chunk raises InvalidInputFormat → no chunks → []. ✓.\n\nFor UBIFS truncation test: find_chunks with content = sb + less than needed → chunk past EOF dropped → []. Let me check search_chunks drops past-EOF chunks... In unblob's finder, chunks with end_offset > file size are removed (remove_inner_chunks/... there's a check). Let me verify quickly in finder.py."]},"started_at_ms":1794660607085,"completed_at_ms":1794660659184}}
