{"timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:52:53.812Z","ordinal":455,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d9fc-8ce9-7420-953c-6c7a3fab8a59","turn_id":"01a1d9fc-8cfb-7500-aadc-dd421289bedc","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_aa8a13d7618ca3d8f5068450","summary_text":[],"raw_content":["27 个单元测试全过。现在做集成测试夹具：多卷 + 坏块的 UBI 镜像。写生成脚本，生成镜像，验证 ubireader 能提取，然后跑集成测试生成期望输出。\n\nFixture: `tests/integration/filesystem/ubi/ubi/__input__/multi-volume-bad-blocks.ubi`\n\n设计（PEB 1024, vid_hdr_offset 64, data_offset 128, image_seq 自定）:\n- PEB0: layout volume lnum 0 (vtbl: rec0 empty, rec1 \"alpha\" vol_id 1 dynamic reserved 2, rec2 \"beta\" vol_id 2 dynamic reserved 2)\n- PEB1: layout volume lnum 1 (copy)\n- PEB2: alpha LEB0: \"alpha-file-1\\n\"\n- PEB3: BAD (garbage, 0x00? 用随机垃圾更像坏块——用无效 EC 头 + 0xEE 填充）\n- PEB4: alpha LEB1: \"alpha-file-2\\n\"\n- PEB5: beta LEB0: \"beta-file-1\\n\"\n- PEB6: BAD\n- PEB7: beta LEB1: \"beta-file-2\\n\"\n\nvtbl rec: reserved_pebs=2, alignment=1, data_pad=0, vol_type=1 (dynamic), upd_marker=0, name_len, name (128s), flags=0, padding 23s, crc = ~crc32(first 168).\n\nVID hdr: magic UBI!, version 1, vol_type 1, copy_flag 0, compat 5, vol_id, lnum, padding 4s(0), data_size, used_ebs, data_pad, data_crc, padding2 12s? wait format: '>4sBBBBII4sIIII4sQ12sI' → magic, version, vol_type, copy_flag, compat, vol_id(I), lnum(I), padding(4s), data_size(I), used_ebs(I), data_pad(I), data_crc(I), padding2(4s), sqnum(Q), padding3(12s), hdr_crc(I) = 64 bytes.\n\nLayout volume VID: vol_id = 0x7fffefff, lnum 0/1, data_size = vtbl size (2*172? fruits had data_size 0... hmm fruits layout VID data_size=0. But real ubinize sets data_size = vtbl size. ubireader reads vtbl from data_offset regardless. I'll set data_size = 172*2 = 344? Hmm, UBI_VTBL_REC_SZ... number of records = up to 128. ubinize writes vtbl of UBI_MAX_VOLUMES(128) records? The layout volume reserved_pebs... fruits used 2 records + zeros. I'll write 128 records (2 used, rest zeros)? data area is 1024-128=896 bytes < 128*172. fruits wrote 2 records (344 bytes) in 896-byte data area. ubireader reads vtbl_recs from... let me check how many records ubireader reads: probably UBI_MAX_VOLUMES or until... Let me check ubireader/ubi/volume or __init__ get_vtbl_recs: reads `vtbl_recs` from block data, count = UBI_MAX_VOLUMES? If it tries to read 128 recs * 172 = 22016 bytes from an 896-byte data area... fruits works, so it must handle it. Let me check ubireader source quickly.\n\nActually simplest: mimic fruits.ubi exactly — it works. 2 vtbl records at data offset, data_size=0 in layout VID hdr, zeros elsewhere.\n\nWait, fruits had 3 records? rec0 empty at 128, rec1 apple at 300, rec2 data at 472. Vol IDs: apple=1 (index 1), data=2 (index 2). So record index = vol_id. I'll do same: rec0 empty, rec1 \"alpha\", rec2 \"beta\".\n\ndata_crc for volume PEBs: ~crc32(data[:data_size]).\n\nFor dynamic volumes, ubireader writes data_size bytes per LEB to the .ubifs output. Expected output files: img-<seq>_vol-alpha.ubifs = \"alpha-file-1\\n\" + \"alpha-file-2\\n\" (13+13=26 bytes?), beta similarly.\n\nHmm wait — will the .ubifs outputs then be scanned by UBIFSHandler? They don't start with UBIFS superblock → unknown files, stay as-is. Like fruits test. Good.\n\nBut I'd ALSO like the integration test to prove \"按卷解出 UBIFS 并提取文件\" with real UBIFS volumes + bad blocks. The orange test covers real UBIFS volumes (but truncated, no bad blocks). Building a real UBIFS-in-UBI multi-volume image with bad blocks requires mkfs.ubifs... Can I embed real UBIFS? I could take the existing banana.zlib.ubifs (a real UBIFS image, leb_size 126976, 14 LEBs = 1.7MB) and wrap it in a UBI image with PEB size 131072 (leb 126976 + 4096 hdr space... data_offset must be ≥ 4096? For PEB 131072, min_io 2048: vid_hdr_offset=2048, data_offset=4096, leb_size = 131072-4096 = 126976 ✓ matches banana's leb_size!). So: build UBI image: PEB0/1 layout (vtbl: volume \"banana\" reserved 14 PEBs, dynamic), PEB2..15 = banana LEBs 0..13 (each LEB = 126976 bytes from banana.zlib.ubifs, prefixed with VID hdr at offset 2048? wait — VID header goes at vid_hdr_offset=2048, EC header at 0, data (LEB content) at data_offset=4096. PEB size 131072.\n\nAnd insert a bad PEB in the middle (say between LEB5 and LEB6 — unallocated) plus make volume reserved_pebs=14. Then unblob should carve the whole thing, ubireader extracts img-..._vol-banana.ubifs, and UBIFSHandler extracts banana1-4.txt. That's a full end-to-end \"坏块+按卷提取 UBIFS\" test! Size: 17 PEBs * 128KiB ≈ 2.2MB. Similar to orange (3.4MB). OK.\n\nBut wait — VID hdr data_size for each LEB: UBIFS LEBs in UBI images: vid hdr data_size = used bytes? For UBIFS volumes (dynamic), data_size = leb_size? ubinize sets data_size to the amount of data in the PEB... For the last LEB maybe less. ubireader writes data_size bytes per LEB when building the .ubifs? If it writes only data_size bytes, the extracted .ubifs would be shorter than leb_size*leb_cnt → UBIFS chunk past EOF → dropped! Hmm. How does ubireader_extract_images write UBIFS volumes? For dynamic volumes it writes `data_size` bytes... Actually let me check: ubireader/ubi/__init__.py or image.py — the extraction writes block.data which is data_size bytes? If so, real ubinize images have data_size = leb_size for all UBIFS LEBs? Not necessarily — ubinize sets data_size to actual data length per LEB... Hmm, but then how does ubireader produce a valid .ubifs from real images (orange test works: vol-configuration.ubifs got extracted)? Let me look at ubireader's image extraction code.\n\nLet me check how the orange image's VID data_size fields look and what ubireader writes."]},"started_at_ms":1794660733354,"completed_at_ms":1794660773812}}
