(26 bytes) → not UBIFS → stays as carved file. Hmm — but wait, will unblob's UBIFSHandler match inside vol-banana.ubifs? Yes at 0. Good.\n\nvtbl rec: reserved_pebs: banana=14, config=2. alignment=1, data_pad=0, vol_type=1, upd_marker=0, name_len, name 128s, flags 0, padding 23s, crc.\n\nLayout VID hdr: vol_id 0x7fffefff, lnum 0/1, vol_type 1, compat 5, data_size = 172*2? fruits used 0. ubinize uses data_size = UBI_VTBL_REC_SZ * UBI_MAX_VOLUMES? Hmm. ubireader reads vtbl via `get_vtbl_recs` — let me just check what it reads: ubireader/ubi/block/layout.py probably reads vtbl_recs from data of layout blocks: `vtbl_recs(data)` reads as many records as fit? Let me check defines.vtbl_recs usage. To be safe, mimic fruits (data_size=0, 2 recs + zeros padding to fill data area? fruits data area 896 bytes: 2 recs (344) + zeros). ubireader's get_vtbl_recs: reads UBI_MAX_VOLUMES records? If it reads beyond data... fruits works so whatever it does tolerates short data. I'll write 3 records (indices 0,1,2) + zero-pad rest of data area.\n\nWait, actually for banana volume I need reserved_pebs in vtbl rec — does ubireader use reserved_pebs? Probably only for display. Volume size comes from found blocks. OK.\n\nLet me check ubireader's get_vtbl_recs quickly, then write the generator."]},"started_at_ms":1794660791989,"completed_at_ms":1794660812789}}
