{"timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:58:07.529Z","ordinal":621,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1d9fc-8ce9-7420-953c-6c7a3fab8a59","turn_id":"01a1d9fc-8cfb-7500-aadc-dd421289bedc","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_662f1e2420e40640ec9a9c4d","summary_text":[],"raw_content":["Confirmed: the rar failure is because LFS fixtures aren't fetched (1508 files are pointers). Not related to my change. \n\nShould I bulk-fetch all 1508 LFS files? At ~0.3-1.5s each, that's 10-40 minutes. It would let me run the full suite. Alternatively, run the full suite excluding tests that need LFS fixtures... most integration tests need them. \n\nA more targeted approach: run the full test suite but understand that LFS-dependent failures are environmental. Better: fetch all LFS files in parallel with xargs -P. Let me do that — it makes the workspace properly set up (AGENTS.md even says to run `git lfs pull`; this is the equivalent). With -P 16 it should take a few minutes.\n\nLet me write the fetch script to a file (AGENTS.md: save scripts run more than once) and run it in background while I do remaining work (README check, commit message summary). Actually let me just run it and wait."]},"started_at_ms":1794661087528,"completed_at_ms":1794661087529}}
